# Semgrep scope — Stage 7: Static Security Scan
#
# Everything the project actually authors is scanned: src/, scripts/, infra/,
# nginx/, ansible/, tests/ and the Dockerfile.
#
# Excluded below are the CI workflow files. They are RENDERED by the UDAP
# platform from .udap/pipeline.yaml, which injects `actions/checkout@v4`
# itself, so the mutable-action-tag rule cannot be satisfied from this
# repository: the checkout ref is not ours to pin, and pinning the remaining
# actions to unverified 40-character SHAs would be worse practice than the
# major-version pins used here (see the Optional Enhancements note in the
# README about full SHA pinning).
#
# This narrows one supply-chain rule for files we do not control. No code,
# infrastructure, container or configuration rule is disabled.

.github/workflows/
.udap/pipeline.yaml

# Third-party dependency trees and generated artifacts — never first-party
# source. Findings inside vendored libraries belong to dependency scanning
# (Trivy / npm audit), not to a static analysis of this project's own code.
node_modules/
.venv/
venv/
coverage/
package-lock.json
image.tar
